{"lines":[{"t":"Test 4","x":0.069548872779612914,"y":0.075581395051709577,"h":0.015988372635703185,"w":0.062030073801676439,"c":1},{"h":0.04815846754517461,"t":"But over the past few decades, it has become clear this wasn't such a bright idea.","x":0.11577920442156606,"y":0.1042724564662556,"w":0.80191233317057276,"c":1},{"h":0.050145499873606503,"x":0.11582258411632172,"w":0.77777750651041666,"c":1,"t":"Chemical fertilisers can release polluting nitrous oxide into the atmosphere and","y":0.12412743186746444},{"c":1,"h":0.048075143552486654,"w":0.77180618286132807,"x":0.11589185071120994,"y":0.14594175918338181,"t":"excess is often washed away with the rain, releasing nitrogen into rivers. More"},{"y":0.17035578616334246,"w":0.7753888956705729,"c":1,"t":"recently, we have found that indiscriminate use of fertilisers hurts the soil itself,","h":0.040729027752406388,"x":0.11589629950223904},{"y":0.19165248015703562,"h":0.041249286875138291,"t":"turning it acidic and salty, and degrading the soil they are supposed to nourish.","w":0.77715423583984378,"c":1,"x":0.11600407426014726},{"h":0.041649901321912153,"t":"One of the people looking for a solution to this problem is Pius Floris, who started","x":0.11610590494243751,"w":0.79789204915364575,"c":1,"y":0.22154014547208267},{"x":0.11787198895462155,"t":"out running a tree-care business in the Netherlands, and now advises some of the","w":0.80166951497395833,"c":1,"y":0.24368686876012369,"h":0.037441670011875261},{"y":0.26570256660511427,"w":0.80156468709309903,"c":1,"h":0.035442342469558685,"t":"world's top soil scientists. He came to realise that the best way to ensure his trees","x":0.11793321941031565},{"y":0.28566922119078553,"t":"flourished was to take care of the soil, and has developed a cocktail of beneficial","w":0.79039276123046887,"x":0.11795849497623816,"c":1,"h":0.037501537178073918},{"y":0.30634683871036461,"w":0.80719258626302082,"h":0.035717700729812285,"x":0.11982882295601371,"c":1,"t":"bacteria, fungi and humus* to do this. Researchers at the University of Valladolid in"},{"c":1,"h":0.031444210585516164,"y":0.32929845248381362,"t":"Spain recently used this cocktail on soils destroyed by years of fertiliser overuse.","x":0.11996104626470667,"w":0.79185953776041651},{"t":"When they applied Floris's mix to the desert-like test plots, a good crop of plants","x":0.11993127059709262,"w":0.78450393676757824,"y":0.34963428584282141,"h":0.031714296310238144,"c":1},{"x":0.12002404885567226,"c":1,"y":0.37163778768578037,"t":"emerged that were not just healthy at the surface, but had roots strong enough to","h":0.029170899105624759,"w":0.79374465942382799},{"h":0.02816907559681614,"c":1,"x":0.12000583732300962,"w":0.78435582478841148,"y":0.39298492685549824,"t":"pierce dirt as hard as rock. The few plants that grew in the control plots, fed with"},{"t":"traditional fertilisers, were small and weak.","y":0.41935480233989808,"x":0.11821997406498687,"w":0.41578809102376302,"h":0.024354432370688794,"c":1},{"y":0.44646485490025389,"t":"However, measures like this are not enough to solve the global soil degradation","x":0.11826705787824854,"w":0.78042180379231774,"c":1,"h":0.026770034760563055},{"t":"problem. To assess our options on a global scale we first need an accurate picture","x":0.1182383222073948,"w":0.80486348470052083,"h":0.025286781964421801,"y":0.46794254846364769,"c":1},{"y":0.48884872920037681,"h":0.024980477494573217,"c":1,"w":0.81231592814127607,"x":0.11829287491362417,"t":"of what types of soil are out there, and the problems they face. That's not easy. For"},{"x":0.11834397104769551,"y":0.51083454250777149,"w":0.80844355265299472,"h":0.022026776806892134,"t":"one thing, there is no agreed international system for classifying soil. In an attempt","c":1},{"w":0.80088582356770832,"c":1,"y":0.53182470754151512,"x":0.1183396230750077,"h":0.021774278482313059,"t":"to unify the different approaches, the UN has created the Global Soil Map project."},{"t":"Researchers from nine countries are working together to create a map linked to a","h":0.021802200936380745,"x":0.12023701763737402,"y":0.55181715263344078,"w":0.79523218790690109,"c":1},{"x":0.12030073935599148,"y":0.57405022488213031,"c":1,"w":0.81015040079752598,"h":0.021893110109465597,"t":"database that can be fed measurements from field surveys, drone surveys, satellte"},{"w":0.79135340372721363,"h":0.019038544880215502,"y":0.59433354812649908,"t":"imagery, lab analyses and so on to provide real-time data on the state of the soil.","x":0.1184210424026359,"c":1},{"w":0.7988721720377604,"t":"Within the next four years, they aim to have mapped soils worldwide to a depth of","x":0.1203007559928445,"y":0.61482558140738575,"h":0.018895348808647183,"c":1},{"x":0.12207165544847286,"t":"100 metres, with the results freely accessible to all.","h":0.021594586099107582,"y":0.63397159400035963,"c":1,"w":0.49834523518880214},{"x":0.11447539953431297,"y":0.66305460306758757,"h":0.027579153420767,"c":1,"w":0.77296656290690102,"t":"But this is only a first step. We need ways of presenting the problem that bring"},{"t":"it home to governments and the wider public, says Pamela Chasek at the","y":0.68244891170837352,"w":0.7205741373697917,"h":0.030777237911187583,"x":0.12181958549443674,"c":1},{"x":0.12009105626767905,"y":0.70565353194250058,"t":"International Institute for Sustainable Development, in Winnipeg, Canada. 'Most","c":1,"w":0.78230768839518228,"h":0.027934234678092862},{"t":"scientists don't speak language that policy-makers can understand, and vice versa.","y":0.72395848466495194,"x":0.12378176917587894,"w":0.80687225341796875,"h":0.030502148620251801,"c":1},{"t":"Chasek and her colleagues have proposed a goal of 'zero net land degradation'","x":0.12577851471045334,"y":0.74534501057632807,"h":0.028329229017111546,"w":0.78224660237630217,"c":1},{"h":0.031926798037536952,"y":0.76375555409919671,"w":0.76764277140299475,"t":"Like the idea of carbon neutrality, it is an easily understood target that can help","x":0.12551761699403338,"c":1},{"y":0.78512177892259094,"t":"shape expectations and encourage action.","x":0.12550221043192789,"w":0.41068323771158854,"h":0.024571808706309373,"c":1},{"x":0.12555409668429726,"c":1,"t":"For soils on the brink, that may be too late. Several researchers are agitating for","y":0.81525390620812077,"w":0.77886159261067711,"h":0.031860616847306567},{"y":0.83556741990377759,"h":0.033184482601482657,"x":0.1254222557110713,"c":1,"t":"the immediate creation of protected zones for endangered soils. One difficulty","w":0.75653783162434896},{"y":0.85542947049582918,"x":0.12551677409599743,"w":0.7845206197102863,"h":0.034046295912743219,"c":1,"t":"here is defining what these areas should conserve: areas where the greatest soil"},{"y":0.87552860794574061,"w":0.79946884155273423,"c":1,"t":"diversity is present? Or areas of unspoilt soils that could act as a future benchmark","h":0.032209585500546423,"x":0.12744785585369878},{"t":"of quality?","y":0.89506980942155223,"w":0.098573163350423182,"h":0.019526942806403547,"c":1,"x":0.1274274554782957},{"w":0.74742736816406241,"y":0.9255703952388511,"h":0.037177874975947489,"t":"Whatever we do, if we want our soils to survive, we need to take action now.","c":1,"x":0.12724442870428959}],"w":2400,"h":3106}